{
  "esm": "0.8.0",
  "metadata": {
    "name": "mpas_mesh_level2",
    "description": "MPAS exemplar mesh data, icosahedral level 2 on the unit sphere (R = 1; multiply lengths by R and areas by R^2 for a physical sphere): 162 Voronoi cells, 480 edges, 320 vertices \u2014 the spherical Voronoi diagram of the 162 twice-bisected icosahedron generators (12 pentagonal + 150 hexagonal cells; the bisection of the level-1 generator set of mesh/level1.esm). This is mesh DATA, not a library entry: a section-4.7 subsystem file (one model, no dynamics) whose observed variables carry the connectivity and geometry as literal `const` arrays (esm-spec 4.2 `const`; the document-literal CONST-connectivity convention of ESS tests/valid/aggregate/edge_enumeration_area_eff.esm and tests/valid/geometry/intersect_polygon_planar_ode.esm). Conventions (MPAS / Ringler et al. 2010, all ids 1-based): cellsOnEdge[e] = [c1, c2] with the positive edge normal pointing from c1 to c2; verticesOnEdge[e] = [v1, v2] with the positive tangent from v1 to v2 satisfying t = k x n (k = outward radial), so traversing v1->v2 runs counterclockwise around the cell the normal leaves; edgeSignOnCell[i][k] = +1 where the positive normal of edgesOnCell[i][k] is outward from cell i (i = c1), -1 otherwise; edgesOnCell rows list each cell's edges in counterclockwise order viewed from outside the sphere, zero-padded to maxEdges (padding slots are never dereferenced: the ragged edges_of_cell iteration is bounded by nEdgesOnCell[i]). Geometry: cell centers are the generators, mesh vertices are the circumcenters of the Delaunay triangles, dvEdge/dcEdge are great-circle arc lengths, areaCell is the spherical-polygon area (signed triangle excesses fanned from the generator, compensated per-cell accumulation; the areaCell values sum to 4*pi EXACTLY under correctly-rounded summation, and to < 1e-13 under naive summation). Derivation is exactly reproducible from the golden-ratio icosahedron (0, +/-1, +/-phi) by two rounds of arc bisection and circumcenter duality (the identical pipeline byte-reproduces mesh/level0.esm and reproduces mesh/level1.esm's connectivity exactly / geometry to <= 10 ulp); verified at authoring time: Delaunay empty-circumcircle for every triangle, opposite edgeSignOnCell on the two cells of every edge, and the discrete div-of-curl telescoping identity sum_k sign[i][k]*(eta[v2]-eta[v1]) == 0 exactly for arbitrary integer vertex fields eta. WIDENED CONTRACT (2026-07, regridding wave): latVertex/lonVertex/verticesOnCell added so cell polygon rings are derivable in-document (the conservative regridder consumes [cells, maxEdges, 2] lon-lat vertex rings; see grids/mpas/grid.esm mpas_cell_rings_deg). Derived from THIS FILE's committed bytes by the vertex-duality extension of the original pipeline: each mesh vertex is the circumcenter of its three adjacent generators (adjacency from verticesOnEdge + cellsOnEdge, positions from latCell/lonCell, sign chosen toward the generators), and verticesOnCell[i][k] is the vertex shared by the consecutive CCW edges edgesOnCell[i][k] and edgesOnCell[i][k+1]. Re-verified from the serialized bytes at authoring time: every vertex has exactly 3 incident edges and 3 adjacent cells and sits equidistant from its three generators to < 1e-12 rad; the derived vertex positions reproduce the committed dvEdge great-circle lengths to <= 1.6e-15 rad and the committed areaCell spherical ring areas to <= 6.2e-16 sr; every derived ring is CCW-positive and the compensated ring-area total differs from 4*pi by 0.0e+00.",
    "license": "MIT",
    "tags": [
      "esd:mesh-data",
      "family:mpas",
      "mesh:icosahedral_level2",
      "sphere:unit"
    ],
    "references": [
      {
        "citation": "Ringler, T., Thuburn, J., Klemp, J. B., & Skamarock, W. C. (2010). A unified approach to energy conservation and potential vorticity dynamics for arbitrarily-structured C-grids. Journal of Computational Physics, 229(9), 3065-3090."
      }
    ]
  },
